E["npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde"] = {t="npc",n="Fallen Hero of the Horde",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Fallen Hero of the Horde is the lingering spirit of an orc warrior standing watch on the southern road out of the Swamp of Sorrows. Bound by regret and dishonor, he warns passing travelers of the horrors awaiting them in the Blasted Lands and seeks champions willing to deliver his tortured soldiers from demonic bondage.",h="The Fallen Hero of the Horde is the lingering spirit of an orc warrior standing watch on the southern road...",sec={{t="A Tragic Command",b="In life, this warrior was a celebrated champion dispatched with a handpicked regiment of soldiers to investigate the Blasted Lands and report back on the presence of the Burning Legion. His dispatch never made it; the courier sent north toward Stonard was ambushed and slain by the Swamp Talker and his murlocs. Stranded without orders or reinforcements, the commander eventually marched his soldiers south into the shattered wastes to confront the growing darkness. It was a fatal misjudgment. Overwhelmed by demonic forces, his army was scattered, captured, and subjected to horrific torment at the hands of the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Failure",b="Captured alongside his lieutenant, Kirith, the commander endured brutal torture in the Serpent's Coil while their captors ripped the souls from his surviving men. Escaping only to succumb to his fatal wounds near the swamp's border, the hero's spirit remains tethered to the threshold of the Blasted Lands. His soldiers suffered an even darker fate: their soulless husks were bound to mystic stones, serving as immortal thralls divided between Razelikh and his lieutenants—Archmage Allistarj, Lady Sevine, and Grol the Destroyer. Until their soul-binding stones are shattered and their torment ended, his restless spirit cannot know peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the Fallen Hero in life?",a="He was a veteran orc warrior chosen to lead a reconnaissance force into the Blasted Lands to assess the demonic threat. He died of grievous wounds after escaping torture at the hands of Razelikh the Defiler, leaving his spirit stranded by the road leading out of the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"fallen hero identity","fallen hero name","who is the fallen hero"}},{q="Why is he haunting the border of the Blasted Lands?",a="He is bound by the shame of losing his regiment and failing his mission. He refuses to pass on until brave adventurers venture south to destroy the stones of binding that hold his soldiers in eternal servitude to the Burning Legion.",al={"why is he a ghost","fallen hero ghost","why is he here"}},{q="What happened to the orders he sent to Stonard?",a="The scout carrying his urgent report back to the outpost of Stonard was ambushed and killed by murlocs in the swamp led by the Swamp Talker. Because the report was lost, reinforcements never arrived, prompting the hero to advance alone into the Blasted Lands.",al={"missing orders","what happened to his orders","swamp talker courier"}},{q="What happened to his lieutenant, Kirith?",a="Lieutenant Kirith suffered demonic experiments within the Serpent's Coil. His soul was warped and twisted, turning his physical form into a monstrous felhunter lurking in the depths of the cave.",al={"lieutenant kirith","who is kirith","what happened to kirith"},sp=1},{q="Why are his soldiers invulnerable?",a="Razelikh and his lieutenants severed the souls of the captive soldiers from their flesh. Without a soul, their physical bodies cannot truly die. They can only be freed if their bodies are battered near disintegration, rendering the soul-binding stones nearby briefly vulnerable to destruction.",al={"invulnerable soldiers","stones of binding","servants of razelikh"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The hero embodies the agony of a warrior whose honor was stripped away by demonic cruelty, appealing to Horde adventurers to avenge his lost squad and clean the stain of defeat from their legacy.",["class:Warrior"]="As a fallen warrior of renown, his spectral kinship resonates strongly with martial adventurers who understand the sting of surviving when their comrades have fallen."},kw={"allistarj","fallen hero of the horde","grol the destroyer","lieutenant kirith","razelikh the defiler","sevine","stones of binding","swamp talker"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","subzone:serpent-s-coil","subzone:stonard","subzone:dark-portal","topic:burning-legion","topic:horde","topic:murloc"},src={"Fallen Hero of the Horde"}}
E["npc:fel-zerul"] = {t="npc",n="Fel'zerul",z="swampofsorrows",s="Fel'zerul is an orc warlock stationed at Stonard in the murky depths of the Swamp of Sorrows. Acting under direct orders from Warchief Thrall, he investigates the ominous presence lurking within the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",h="Fel'zerul is an orc warlock stationed at Stonard in the murky depths of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Sunken Temple",b="While Thrall's Horde generally views dark arts with suspicion, the Warchief recognizes that understanding sinister powers requires those who study them. Fel'zerul was dispatched to Stonard specifically to unravel the corruption surrounding the Pool of Tears and the submerged Temple of Atal'Hakkar. By directing adventurers to recover artifacts and investigate the exiled Atal'ai trolls, the warlock seeks to determine what evil stirs beneath the murky waters before it threatens the Horde's southern outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fel'zerul?",a="Fel'zerul is an orc warlock residing in Stonard, the Horde's stronghold in the Swamp of Sorrows. He serves as an investigator analyzing the dark rituals unfolding within the nearby Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",al={"felzerul","who is fel'zerul","stonard warlock"}},{q="Why did Thrall send a warlock to Stonard?",a="Warchief Thrall dispatched Fel'zerul because dealing with ancient curses and blood rituals requires expertise in darker sorceries. Fel'zerul's mandate is to monitor the disturbing developments around the sunken temple and protect Horde interests in the swamp.",al={"thrall felzerul","why is felzerul here","felzerul mission"}},{q="What is Fel'zerul investigating?",a="Fel'zerul is investigating the Atal'ai trolls and their profane rites within the Temple of Atal'Hakkar at the Pool of Tears. He enlists scouts and adventurers to dredge up artifacts and track down exiled priests who might hold crucial lore.",al={"felzerul quest lore","what does felzerul want","pool of tears investigation"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Fel'zerul represents an official tasking of a warlock by Thrall, showcasing that the new Horde occasionally relies on practitioners of the dark arts to counter obscure, esoteric threats.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed at Stonard, Fel'zerul acts as an early warning scout, ensuring that whatever dark magic festering in the swamp does not blindside the Horde's foothold in the region."},kw={"atal'hakkar","fel'zerul","felzerul","stonard","swamp of sorrows","thrall","warlock"},rel={"subzone:stonard","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:pool-of-tears","zone:swampofsorrows","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Fel'zerul"}}
E["quest:1389"] = {t="quest",n="Draenethyst Crystals",z="swampofsorrows",s="Magtoor, at the Harborage, asks for six draenethyst crystals, sacred to Magtoor's people and stolen by the lost ones of the Fallow Sanctuary. Without them, Magtoor's people fear they too may lose their way.",h="Magtoor, at the Harborage, asks for six draenethyst crystals, sacred to Magtoor's people and stolen by the...",sec={{t="The Lost Ones",b="The lost ones of the Fallow Sanctuary look as Magtoor's people do, but the rigors of the journey to Azeroth drove them mad. Once brethren, they now dwell in the Sanctuary, to the east, and they seize or kill anyone who strays close. They have also stolen something sacred: draenethyst crystals.",sp=0},{t="Without the Crystals",b="Magtoor's people do not have the strength to enter the Fallow Sanctuary and take the draenethyst back from among the huts and campfires. Without the crystals, they fear they too may lose their way. Magtoor asks you to bring back six.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the draenethyst crystals?",a="Magtoor, who is found at the Harborage.",al={"who gives draenethyst crystals","magtoor quest","who wants draenethyst"}},{q="Why are the draenethyst crystals important to Magtoor?",a="They are sacred to Magtoor's people. Without them, Magtoor fears they too may lose their way.",al={"why draenethyst crystals","what do draenethyst crystals do","draenethyst purpose"}},{q="Who took the crystals?",a="The lost ones of the Fallow Sanctuary, to the east. They were once Magtoor's brethren, until the rigors of the journey to Azeroth drove them mad.",al={"who stole draenethyst","who has the crystals","fallow sanctuary enemies"}},{q="Where can the crystals be found?",a="Among the huts and campfires of the Fallow Sanctuary, which lies to the east.",al={"draenethyst crystal location","where are draenethyst crystals","find draenethyst"}},{q="Why can't Magtoor's people retrieve them themselves?",a="They do not have the strength to enter the Sanctuary and take the crystals back.",al={"why doesn't magtoor fight","why help magtoor"}}},kw={"draenethyst","fallow sanctuary","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:harborage","subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Magtoor",["end"]="Magtoor",level="35",id=1389},src={"Draenethyst Crystals (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1392"] = {t="quest",n="Noboru the Cudgel",z="swampofsorrows",s="For months, Noboru has tormented the Draenei at the Harborage. Noboru's cudgel stands as a mark of the cruelty the lost ones have dealt them, and you are asked to bring it to the leader of the Harborage.",h="For months, Noboru has tormented the Draenei at the Harborage.",sec={{t="A Symbol of Brutality",b="Noboru has tormented the Harborage's Draenei for months. The cudgel has come to stand for the cruelty the lost ones have dealt them. With it in hand, you carry it to the leader of the Harborage.",sp=0},{t="Magtoor's Welcome",b="Magtoor asks whether the weapon means Noboru is dead, and calls this a day of joy there. Noboru and his gang terrorized the Draenei, wandering the swamps and killing any who crossed their path. Noboru threatened their very survival, and they lacked the strength to face him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Noboru?",a="One of the lost ones, who has tormented the Harborage's Draenei for months.",al={"who is noboru","noboru lore","noboru cudgel guy"}},{q="Why does the Harborage want Noboru's cudgel?",a="The cudgel stands for the cruelty that the lost ones have dealt the Draenei of the Harborage.",al={"why turn in the cudgel","noboru cudgel purpose","why bring cudgel to magtoor"}},{q="Who receives the cudgel?",a="Magtoor, who leads the Harborage.",al={"who is magtoor","where does the cudgel go"}},{q="Where is the Harborage located?",a="In the Swamp of Sorrows, where the Draenei of the Harborage live.",al={"where is harborage","harborage location"}}},kw={"cudgel","draenei","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","noboru","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:harborage"},m={start="Noboru's Cudgel",["end"]="Magtoor",level="39",faction="Neutral",id=1392},src={"Noboru the Cudgel (quest)"}}
E["quest:1393"] = {t="quest",n="Galen's Escape",z="swampofsorrows",s="Galen Goodward is in the Fallow Sanctuary, begging for rescue from the creatures there, and promises a great treasure to anyone who gets him out. It waits in a locked strongbox at his camp north of Stonard.",h="Galen Goodward is in the Fallow Sanctuary, begging for rescue from the creatures there, and promises a great...",sec={{t="A Plea for Rescue",b="Galen Goodward cries out that the creatures around him are going to eat him. Anyone who helps him out of danger is promised a great treasure. It sits at his camp, out in the swamp north of Stonard, locked in a strongbox that opens only through a trick known to Galen alone. If you help him escape, he will teach it to you.",sp=0},{t="At the Strongbox",b="At the camp you find the strongbox's keyhole filled with black resin, so it cannot be opened that way. But Galen told you of a latch hidden on the bottom of the box. A quick search finds it, and flipping it opens the strongbox.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Galen Goodward?",a="Someone held in the Fallow Sanctuary who fears the creatures there will eat them, and who offers a great treasure to anyone who helps them escape.",al={"who is galen","galen goodward lore","galens escape guy"}},{q="Where is Galen's camp located?",a="In the swamp north of Stonard, in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"where is galens camp","galens strongbox location","where is the strongbox"}},{q="Why can't the strongbox be opened in the usual way?",a="Galen's treasure is locked in a strongbox that opens only through a trick that Galen alone knows, which Galen will teach to whoever helps him escape.",al={"how to open strongbox","galen chest key"}}},kw={"black resin","fallow sanctuary","galen goodward","galen's escape","stonard","strongbox","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stonard"},m={start="Galen Goodward",["end"]="Galen's Strongbox",level="38",id=1393},src={"Galen's Escape"}}
E["quest:1396"] = {t="quest",n="Encroaching Wildlife",z="swampofsorrows",s="Watcher Biggs was bound for the eastern coast with a caravan when the lost ones attacked. Biggs alone survived, and now wild creatures skulk near the camp. Biggs asks for your help defending it. This follows Help Watcher Biggs.",h="Watcher Biggs was bound for the eastern coast with a caravan when the lost ones attacked.",sec={{t="A Camp Under Watch",b="The caravan of Watcher Biggs was bound for the eastern coast, but it never arrived. Lost Ones attacked, killing the guards and smashing the supplies, and Biggs alone survived. Biggs has sworn to protect what supplies remain, yet wild creatures skulk close to the camp. Biggs wants you to help defend it.",sp=0},{t="The Creatures Nearby",b="Biggs names three kinds of creature pressing near the camp: young sawtooth crocolisks, sorrow spinners and swamp jaguars. Eight crocolisks, ten spinners and ten jaguars are to be slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where was Watcher Biggs's caravan traveling?",a="To the eastern coast, but the caravan never reached its goal.",al={"where was biggs going","caravan destination","biggs caravan route"}},{q="Who attacked Watcher Biggs's caravan?",a="Lost Ones. They killed the guards and smashed the supplies, and Biggs alone survived.",al={"who attacked biggs","who destroyed the caravan","caravan ambush"}},{q="What beasts threaten the camp?",a="Young sawtooth crocolisks, sorrow spinners and swamp jaguars skulk near it.",al={"which beasts are encroaching","what animals attack biggs","swamp beasts"}},{q="Why does Watcher Biggs remain at the camp?",a="Biggs has sworn to protect the supplies that remain from the caravan.",al={"why is biggs staying","why not flee","biggs supplies"}}},kw={"caravan","lost ones","sawtooth crocolisk","sorrow spinner","supplies","swamp jaguar","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","quest:1421"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=1396},src={"Encroaching Wildlife"}}
E["quest:1398"] = {t="quest",n="Driftwood",z="swampofsorrows",s="After The Lost Caravan, Watcher Biggs still has a wagon to mend before reaching Nethergarde. Biggs needs strong, dry wood, and sends you east to the coast to search for driftwood dried by the sun.",h="After The Lost Caravan, Watcher Biggs still has a wagon to mend before reaching Nethergarde.",sec={{t="Wood for the Wagon",b="Watcher Biggs says you are owed great thanks, and asks for your help once more. If Biggs is ever to reach Nethergarde, the wagon must be fixed, and that takes strong, dry wood. Wood from the swamp's trees is spongy and tangled, and will not do.",sp=0},{t="Driftwood from the Coast",b="Biggs sends you east to the coast, to search for driftwood that the sun has dried. Eight pieces are to be brought back to Biggs in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Watcher Biggs need wood?",a="The wagon must be fixed if Biggs is ever to reach Nethergarde, and wood from the swamp's trees is too spongy and tangled.",al={"driftwood reason","why does biggs need driftwood","why driftwood"}},{q="Where does Watcher Biggs send you for the wood?",a="East to the coast, to search for driftwood that the sun has dried.",al={"driftwood location","where to find driftwood","where is the wood"}},{q="What came before this?",a="The Lost Caravan comes first, and Biggs then asks for more help.",al={"driftwood previous quest","what leads to driftwood","what quest comes before driftwood"}},{q="How much driftwood is needed?",a="Eight pieces of sundried driftwood.",al={"driftwood count","how many driftwood"}},{q="What comes after gathering the driftwood?",a="Deliver the Shipment follows.",al={"driftwood follow up","what is after driftwood","driftwood next quest"}}},kw={"driftwood","nethergarde","sundried driftwood","swamp of sorrows","wagon","watcher biggs"},rel={"quest:1421","quest:1425","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="42",faction="Alliance",id=1398},src={"Driftwood (quest)"}}
E["quest:1418"] = {t="quest",n="Neeka Bloodscar",z="swampofsorrows",s="Helgrum the Swift sends you from Stonard to the Badlands outpost of Kargath, to speak with its head scout, Neeka Bloodscar. Word between Stonard and Kargath is often cut.",h="Helgrum the Swift sends you from Stonard to the Badlands outpost of Kargath, to speak with its head scout...",sec={{t="A Cut Line",b="The Badlands are harsh country and lie close to Loch Modan, which the Alliance holds. Because of this, word between Stonard and Kargath is often cut. Helgrum asks you to prove yourself by travelling to the Badlands and speaking with Neeka Bloodscar, who is head scout there. Neeka's report is then to be sent back to Helgrum.",sp=0},{t="Neeka's Answer",b="Neeka tells you an outrunner was sent toward Stonard barely three days earlier. If Stonard has nothing from Neeka, that runner must have failed. Neeka hopes the next one has more skill, or more luck.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Helgrum the Swift send you?",a="From Stonard to the outpost of Kargath in the Badlands, to speak with Neeka Bloodscar.",al={"where do i go","neeka bloodscar location","where is neeka"}},{q="Why is communication between Stonard and Kargath cut off?",a="The Badlands are harsh and lie close to Loch Modan, which the Alliance holds, and word between Stonard and Kargath is often cut.",al={"why are communications cut","badlands communication problem","why stonard to kargath"}},{q="Who is Neeka Bloodscar?",a="Neeka Bloodscar is the head scout of the Kargath outpost in the Badlands.",al={"who is neeka","neeka role","neeka bloodscar lore"}},{q="What comes after speaking with Neeka Bloodscar?",a="Report to Helgrum follows.",al={"what next","follow up quest","after neeka bloodscar"}}},kw={"badlands","head scout","helgrum the swift","kargath","loch modan","neeka bloodscar","stonard","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:kargath","subzone:stonard","zone:badlands","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:lochmodan","quest:1420","topic:alliance"},m={start="Helgrum the Swift",["end"]="Neeka Bloodscar",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1418},src={"Neeka Bloodscar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1421"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Caravan",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Encroaching Wildlife, Watcher Biggs has a further matter for you. Stunned in the Lost Ones' attack on the caravan, Biggs still saw a wagon hauled off to the Fallow Sanctuary, the Lost Ones' village in the north. A chest of valuable reagents rode in it, and Biggs wants those reagents brought back.",h="After Encroaching Wildlife, Watcher Biggs has a further matter for you.",sec={{t="The Stolen Wagon",b="Biggs was knocked senseless in the attack, yet glimpsed one of the caravan's wagons being dragged away to the Fallow Sanctuary, the Lost Ones' village to the north. In that wagon was a chest of reagents prized by the wizards of Nethergarde Keep for their studies. Biggs wants the chest found and its contents carried back.",sp=0},{t="Word from Biggs",b="Back with the reagents, you find Biggs pleased, for the wizards of Nethergarde can now carry on with their work. Biggs does not know what that work is, only that it has to do with the Dark Portal, over in the Blasted Lands and matters greatly to keeping the Alliance secure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Watcher Biggs?",a="Watcher Biggs lost a wagon of the caravan to the Lost Ones and wants the reagents it carried recovered.",al={"watcher biggs","who gives the lost caravan"}},{q="Where did the Lost Ones take the caravan chest?",a="Biggs saw the wagon hauled away to the Fallow Sanctuary, the Lost Ones' village in the north, with the chest aboard.",al={"caravan chest location","where is fallow sanctuary","where are the reagents"}},{q="Why are the reagents important?",a="The wizards of Nethergarde Keep depend on them for their studies.",al={"why reagents matter","nethergarde reagents purpose"}},{q="What comes after recovering the chest?",a="Driftwood follows once Biggs has the reagents.",al={"next quest after lost caravan","lost caravan chain"}}},kw={"dark portal","fallow sanctuary","lost ones","nethergarde keep","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs","wizards reagents"},rel={"subzone:fallow-sanctuary","subzone:nethergarde-keep","quest:1396","subzone:dark-portal","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Watcher Biggs",level="35",faction="Alliance",id=1421},src={"The Lost Caravan"}}
E["quest:1422"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Lack of Surplus, Tok'Kar begins work on your weapon and tells you to speak with Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows. Katar has said patrols along the beach could use some help.",h="After Lack of Surplus, Tok'Kar begins work on your weapon and tells you to speak with Katar in the Swamp of...",sec={{t="A Word with Katar",b="While working on your weapon, Tok'Kar suggests you talk to Katar, who has said patrols along the beach could use some help. Tok'Kar shares the camp with some louses who drink, and would rather see you keep your wits sharp and your weapons ready than join them.",sp=0},{t="Over the Roar of the Sea",b="Katar asks you for a moment of silence. Above the sea's dull roar, the disgusting gurgling of the fish men can still be heard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Tok'Kar send you to Katar?",a="Tok'Kar is busy with your weapon, and would rather you kept your wits and arms ready than got drunk with the louses sharing the camp.",al={"why talk to katar","tok'kar reason","why visit katar"}},{q="What does Katar need assistance with?",a="Katar has remarked that the patrols along the beach could use some help, and that is what Katar is after.",al={"katar problem","what does katar want","katar patrol"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="It follows Lack of Surplus, after which Tok'Kar begins work on your weapon.",al={"previous quest","prereq","threat from the sea chain"}}},kw={"beach","katar","patrol","shore","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea","tok'kar"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Tok'Kar",["end"]="Katar",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1422},src={"Threat From the Sea"}}
E["quest:1423"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Supplies",z="swampofsorrows",s="A small, sturdy barrel has its seams sealed with pungent yellow wax. A stamp on its base names Quartermaster Lungertz and Nethergarde Keep, and that is where it belongs.",h="A small, sturdy barrel has its seams sealed with pungent yellow wax.",sec={{t="A Stamped Barrel",b="Pungent yellow wax seals the seams of this compact, stout barrel. Underneath, a stamp reads Quartermaster Lungertz, Nethergarde Keep, so the barrel is meant for the quartermaster there.",sp=0},{t="Word from the Quartermaster",b="Quartermaster Lungertz thanks you. Supplies go astray all the way from Darkshire to Nethergarde, and it is good to see some recovered.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is meant to receive the lost supplies?",a="The barrel is marked for Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep.",al={"who gets the barrel","lost supplies recipient","where does the barrel go"}},{q="How can you tell who owns the barrel?",a="The base of the barrel carries a stamp naming Quartermaster Lungertz and Nethergarde Keep.",al={"barrel markings","how to read barrel","quartermaster lungertz stamp"}},{q="What does the barrel look like?",a="It is a small, sturdy barrel with pungent yellow wax along its seams.",al={"lost supplies barrel","barrel description"}}},kw={"barrel","darkshire","lost supplies","nethergarde keep","quartermaster lungertz","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:darkshire"},m={start="Lost Supplies (starter)",["end"]="Quartermaster Lungertz",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=1423},src={"The Lost Supplies"}}
E["quest:1424"] = {t="quest",n="Pool of Tears",z="swampofsorrows",s="In Stonard, Fel'zerul asks you to search around the Pool of Tears for Atal'ai artifacts. The Warchief sent Fel'zerul's people to look into strange events at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, and they arrived to find it sunk.",h="In Stonard, Fel'zerul asks you to search around the Pool of Tears for Atal'ai artifacts.",sec={{t="The Sunken Temple",b="The Atal'ai trolls are dark casters, a tribe notorious for forbidden magic. When Fel'zerul's party reached the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, they were astonished to find it sunk. Green dragons now watch over the place and call themselves protectors of Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Pieces of a Puzzle",b="Fel'zerul wants to learn what happened, and asks you to range around the Pool of Tears gathering Atal'ai artifacts, from which the puzzle can begin to fit together. Nobody knows what dark rites were practised in the temple, only that great magical forces were used. Fel'zerul hopes the Atal'ai's spells may prove useful to the Horde, and wants to understand what the trolls hoped to achieve and what went so horribly wrong.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fel'zerul?",a="Fel'zerul is in Stonard, one of those the Warchief sent to investigate odd goings-on at the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.",al={"fel'zerul","felzerul","who gives pool of tears"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in the Atal'ai trolls?",a="Fel'zerul points out that great magical forces were used there, and thinks the Atal'ai's spells may prove useful to the Horde.",al={"why horde wants atal'ai","atal'ai magic horde"}},{q="Where are the Atal'ai artifacts located?",a="They lie on the bed of the Pool of Tears, near the temple.",al={"atal'ai artifact location","where to find artifacts","pool of tears artifacts"}},{q="Who guards the sunken temple now?",a="Green dragons watch over the place and call themselves protectors of Azeroth.",al={"why are green dragons here","green dragons temple of atal'hakkar","green dragons swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What comes next after the artifacts are delivered?",a="The Atal'ai Exile follows.",al={"next quest after pool of tears","pool of tears follow up","what after pool of tears"}}},kw={"artifacts","atal'ai","fel'zerul","green dragons","pool of tears","stonard","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar","warchief"},rel={"subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:stonard","npc:fel-zerul","quest:1429","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={start="Fel'zerul",["end"]="Fel'zerul",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1424},src={"Pool of Tears (Horde)"}}
E["quest:1425"] = {t="quest",n="Deliver the Shipment",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Driftwood, Watcher Biggs has one last job for you while the wagon is being repaired. Biggs has packed up the key supplies rescued from the ogre attacks and wants you to carry them to Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep.",h="After Driftwood, Watcher Biggs has one last job for you while the wagon is being repaired.",sec={{t="A Last Delivery for Biggs",b="While Biggs repairs the wagon, the key supplies rescued from the ogre attacks have been packed up for you to carry to Nethergarde Keep. The keep stands in the Blasted Lands' northern hills, watching over the Dark Portal. Biggs gives the route: follow the road east, head south into the Blasted Lands where it branches, and turn left at the next fork, with a warning to be wary.",sp=0},{t="At Nethergarde",b="Quartermaster Lungertz is startled to receive a package from Biggs' caravan, since the keep had given up the caravan and Biggs for lost. Lungertz thanks you and hopes the supplies hold Azoran Crystals, a much-needed reagent whose stock at the keep is running low.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the shipment to Nethergarde?",a="Watcher Biggs, who stays to repair the wagon, packed up key supplies rescued from the ogre attacks.",al={"who gives deliver the shipment","deliver the shipment quest giver","watcher biggs delivery"}},{q="Where does this shipment need to go?",a="It goes to Quartermaster Lungertz at Nethergarde Keep, in the Blasted Lands' northern hills.",al={"where is nethergarde keep","how to get to nethergarde","quartermaster lungertz location"}},{q="What comes directly before this delivery?",a="It follows Driftwood.",al={"deliver the shipment prerequisite","what quest comes before deliver the shipment"}},{q="What route leads from the swamp to the keep?",a="Follow the road east, turn south into the Blasted Lands where the road branches, then take the left at the next fork.",al={"directions to nethergarde keep","path to blasted lands"}},{q="What is Nethergarde Keep watching over?",a="It keeps watch over the Dark Portal.",al={"purpose of nethergarde keep","why is nethergarde in blasted lands"}}},kw={"azoran crystals","blasted lands","dark portal","nethergarde keep","quartermaster lungertz","shipment","swamp of sorrows","watcher biggs"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:dark-portal"},m={start="Watcher Biggs",["end"]="Quartermaster Lungertz",level="42",faction="Alliance",id=1425},src={"Deliver the Shipment"}}
E["quest:1426"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="After Tok'Kar sends you to speak with Katar, Katar makes plain a hatred of the sea. Watching the fish men die at the hands of anyone who does the Horde's will gives Katar some pleasure, and Katar asks how many you can slay and whether you would test yourself against their strongest kind.",h="After Tok'Kar sends you to speak with Katar, Katar makes plain a hatred of the sea.",sec={{t="A Grudge Against the Sea",b="Katar bears no affection for the sea or for any creature that comes out of it, and calls it a mistress strong but blind, callous and brutal. Killing the fish men by the hundreds would delight Katar, were it possible, and watching them fall to those who serve the Horde gives a little satisfaction. Katar, in the Swamp of Sorrows, asks you to slay marsh murlocs, marsh inkspewers and marsh flesheaters.",sp=0},{t="Katar's Verdict",b="On your return, Katar says the sea may seem vast and relentless, yet her own offspring now bear your bloody mark. The fish men now know pain and must rebuild their ranks, which Katar finds good, and Katar will smile each time one is silenced. Katar invites you back to slay more.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Katar want the murlocs destroyed?",a="Katar bears no love for the sea or what comes out of it, and would gladly see the fish men slain by the hundreds. Watching them die to those who do the Horde's will gives some pleasure.",al={"why kill murlocs","katar murlocs","why hate sea"}},{q="Where does this hunt take place?",a="In the Swamp of Sorrows, among marsh murlocs, marsh inkspewers and marsh flesheaters.",al={"where are the marsh murlocs","threat from the sea location"}},{q="Who gives this hunt?",a="Katar, whom Tok'Kar sent you to speak with in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"who gives threat from the sea","threat from the sea questgiver"}},{q="What comes before this hunt?",a="It follows the first Threat From the Sea, in which Tok'Kar sent you to speak with Katar.",al={"threat from the sea prerequisite","threat from the sea previous quest"}}},kw={"katar","marsh flesheater","marsh inkspewer","marsh murloc","murloc","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea"},rel={"quest:1422","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc","topic:horde"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Katar",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1426},src={"Threat From the Sea (2)"}}
E["quest:1427"] = {t="quest",n="Threat From the Sea",z="swampofsorrows",s="After your work for Katar, you are told to see Tok'Kar once more before you rest. Katar believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were away, and that one will be offered to you for your help.",h="After your work for Katar, you are told to see Tok'Kar once more before you rest.",sec={{t="Back to Tok'Kar",b="Katar believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were away, and that Tok'Kar will offer you one for your help. Katar adds that you would do well to try its strength on the fish men when ready, though only to please Katar further.",sp=0},{t="Tok'Kar's Thanks",b="Tok'Kar is glad to see you back and says more weapons have been crafted for the war on the murlocs. As thanks for bringing fresh sawtooth meat, and for putting a small smile on Katar's face, he gives you one.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Tok'Kar?",a="Katar does, telling you to see Tok'Kar once more before you rest in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"who gives this quest","where do I get threat from the sea","who starts this"}},{q="Why is Tok'Kar offering a weapon?",a="Katar believes Tok'Kar finished a few weapons while you were gone, and that one will be offered to you in thanks for your help.",al={"why does tok'kar give a weapon","what did tok'kar make","tok'kar reward reason"}},{q="What comes next after speaking with Tok'Kar?",a="Continued Threat follows.",al={"what is the next quest","where to after this","what follows threat from the sea"}}},kw={"katar","murloc","sawtooth meat","swamp of sorrows","threat from the sea","tok'kar"},rel={"quest:1428","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="43",faction="Horde",id=1427},src={"Threat From the Sea (3)"}}
E["quest:1428"] = {t="quest",n="Continued Threat",z="swampofsorrows",s="Katar is pleased that your hatred of the fish men is growing alongside Katar's own, and sends you to hunt further fish men on the beach in the Swamp of Sorrows.",h="Katar is pleased that your hatred of the fish men is growing alongside Katar's own, and sends you to hunt...",sec={{t="More Along the Beach",b="Katar tells you to find more of the fish men along the beach, and to return once you have had enough of fighting. Marsh inkspewers, marsh flesheaters and marsh oracles are the ones wanted. Katar will take no pleasure until the sea and every one of her children is silenced, least of all the repulsive fish men.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Katar, in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"who starts continued threat","continued threat quest giver","katar swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What creatures need to be hunted?",a="Katar wants marsh inkspewers, marsh flesheaters and marsh oracles along the beach.",al={"what to kill continued threat","continued threat targets","which murlocs"}},{q="Why does Katar want the murlocs culled?",a="Katar will take no pleasure until the sea and her brood are silenced, the fish men most of all.",al={"why kill murlocs","katar motive","why hate fish men"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="It follows the previous Threat From the Sea, after which Tok'Kar offered you a weapon.",al={"continued threat prerequisite","previous quest continued threat"}}},kw={"continued threat","fish men","katar","marsh flesheater","marsh inkspewer","marsh oracle","murlocs","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Katar",["end"]="Katar",level="45",faction="Horde",id=1428},src={"Continued Threat"}}
E["quest:1429"] = {t="quest",n="The Atal'ai Exile",z="swampofsorrows",s="While you were at the Pool of Tears, one of Fel'zerul's scouts brought back a scroll inked in blood on dried flesh. Fel'zerul now bundles the artifacts you gathered and sends you far north to the Hinterlands, to find an exiled Atal'ai priest.",h="While you were at the Pool of Tears, one of Fel'zerul's scouts brought back a scroll inked in blood on dried...",sec={{t="A Sentence in Blood",b="The scroll reads as a judicial ruling against a priest of the Atal'ai, a fate worse than death among his own people. He was exiled to live among the Witherbark trolls, far to the north in the Hinterlands. Fel'zerul will bundle the artifacts and sends you to find the exile, discover their true use, and return.",sp=0},{t="The Exile's Words",b="Shown the bundle, the exile names the artifacts as summoning tools of the Atal'ai. He remarks that the disciples of the Chamber of Blood are being led by Jammal'an the Prophet toward their chosen fate, and wonders whether Hakkar has returned to the temple.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Atal'ai Exile?",a="Fel'zerul in Stonard, who bundles the artifacts you gathered and sends you north to the Hinterlands.",al={"who gives the atal'ai exile","atal'ai exile questgiver","who starts the quest"}},{q="Where is the Atal'ai Exile located?",a="In the Hinterlands, living with the Witherbark trolls at the temple of Shadra'Alor.",al={"where is the exile","atal'ai exile location","where to find atal'ai exile"}},{q="What sentence was passed on the priest?",a="A scroll inked in blood on dried flesh condemns the priest to a fate worse than death among the Atal'ai: exile among the Witherbark trolls in the Hinterlands.",al={"why was he banished","what was the sentence","atal'ai exile backstory"}},{q="What are you carrying to the exile?",a="A bundle of the Atal'ai artifacts gathered at the Pool of Tears, whose true use Fel'zerul wants the exile to reveal.",al={"what bundle do you bring","what are the artifacts","atal'ai artifacts purpose"}},{q="What comes directly before this journey?",a="It follows Pool of Tears, where Fel'zerul had you gather Atal'ai artifacts.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what leads to atal'ai exile"}}},kw={"atal'ai exile","fel'zerul","hakkar","hinterlands","jammal'an","pool of tears","shadra'alor","swamp of sorrows","witherbark"},rel={"npc:fel-zerul","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:hinterlands","subzone:pool-of-tears","topic:troll","topic:priest"},m={start="Fel'zerul",["end"]="Atal'ai Exile",level="44",faction="Horde",id=1429},src={"The Atal'ai Exile"}}
E["quest:1430"] = {t="quest",n="Fresh Meat",z="swampofsorrows",s="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Dar says customers in Orgrimmar have a high demand for crawler meat, especially that of the monstrous crawlers. Dar asks you to bring back some of their legs from the coast.",h="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Dar says customers in Orgrimmar have a high demand for crawler meat, especially that...",sec={{t="Crawler Legs for Orgrimmar",b="Dar's customers have a taste for succulent crawler meat, particularly from the monstrous crawlers. Dar promises to make a trip to the coast worth your while if you bring back some of their legs, to be sent on to Orgrimmar. The coast lies east of here, where the creatures scurry over the beaches and into the surf. A cask of wine awaits your success, and Dar means to taste the goods before they ship.",sp=0},{t="A Taste for the Road",b="Dar is pleased with the legs, imagining them perfectly cooked over an open fire. Dar urges you to take a cooked sample along on your travels and swears it is truly delicious.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants crawler meat in the Swamp of Sorrows?",a="Dar, whose customers in Orgrimmar have a high demand for it.",al={"who gives fresh meat","dar quest","who is dar"}},{q="Where are the monstrous crawlers located?",a="On the coast to the east, scurrying over the beaches and into the surf.",al={"crawler location","where are the crawlers","monstrous crawler shore"}},{q="Why does Dar need these specific legs?",a="Dar's customers have a taste for crawler meat, the monstrous crawlers' most of all, and the legs are to be sent back to Orgrimmar.",al={"why crawler meat","what is the meat for","orgrimmar crawler meat"}}},kw={"crawler legs","dar","fresh meat","monstrous crawler","orgrimmar","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:orgrimmar","item:crawler-leg"},m={start="Dar",["end"]="Dar",level="44",faction="Horde",id=1430},src={"Fresh Meat (Swamp of Sorrows)"}}
E["quest:2622"] = {t="quest",n="The Missing Orders",z="swampofsorrows",s="Dispatch Commander Ruag bristles when asked about the missing orders, insisting they were relayed. Ruag says the soldiers carrying them were ambushed by murlocs and only one lived, and sends you to speak with Bengor.",h="Dispatch Commander Ruag bristles when asked about the missing orders, insisting they were relayed.",sec={{t="Ruag's Account",b="Ruag takes offence at the question and insists the orders were relayed. The soldiers sent with them were, Ruag says, ambushed and brutally beaten by murlocs, and only one lived, if that can be called living. The survivor can barely speak, cannot walk and is fed through a tube. To learn what became of the orders, Ruag says, speak with Bengor, who is around here somewhere, and adds a warning to mind what you poke your nose into, lest it get bitten off.",sp=0},{t="Bengor's Halting Words",b="When you find Bengor, only broken scraps of speech come out, and among them you catch the words swamp talker.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sent the orders that went missing?",a="Dispatch Commander Ruag says the orders were relayed with the soldiers sent out, and grows defensive when asked what became of them.",al={"who gave missing orders","who lost the orders"}},{q="What happened to the soldiers carrying the orders?",a="According to Dispatch Commander Ruag, murlocs ambushed and brutally beat them, and only one lived.",al={"what happened to couriers","how were the orders lost"}},{q="Who is Bengor?",a="Bengor is the one survivor of the ambush. He can barely speak, cannot walk and is fed through a tube.",al={"who is the survivor","bengor lore"}},{q="Where can Bengor be found?",a="Dispatch Commander Ruag says only that Bengor is around here somewhere.",al={"bengor location","where is bengor"}}},kw={"ambush","bengor","dispatch commander ruag","missing orders","murloc","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"quest:2623","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Dispatch Commander Ruag",["end"]="Bengor",level="50",faction="Horde",id=2622},src={"The Missing Orders"}}
E["quest:2623"] = {t="quest",n="The Swamp Talker",z="swampofsorrows",s="Bengor can barely speak, but he manages to tell what became of the orders. The dispatch commander gave them, and on the way to the Blasted Lands the group was ambushed by many murlocs. One of them, named Swamp Talker, took the orders from his hands. They must be recovered and brought to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.",h="Bengor can barely speak, but he manages to tell what became of the orders.",sec={{t="Bengor's Broken Account",b="Bengor says the dispatch commander gave out the orders and that his group was on its way to the Blasted Lands when many murlocs ambushed them. One of the murlocs, named Swamp Talker, took the orders from his hands as a spear was thrust into his skull. Bengor manages a word about a cave to the east before passing out. The orders must be recovered and brought to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Hero's Reckoning",b="The Fallen Hero of the Horde finds it worse than imagined. Nineteen of the Hero's men could have been spared agony if the Hero had not acted so irrationally. Powerless to act, the Hero urges you to help those men.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who stole the Warchief's Orders?",a="A murloc named Swamp Talker took the orders from Bengor's hands during the ambush.",al={"who took the orders","who is swamp talker","who stole orders"}},{q="Where did the Swamp Talker go?",a="Bengor's fading words mention a cave to the east.",al={"where is swamp talker","swamp talker location","where is the murloc cave"}},{q="Where were Bengor and his unit heading?",a="They were on their way to the Blasted Lands, carrying orders from the dispatch commander, when the murlocs ambushed them.",al={"bengor destination","where was bengor going","bengor unit goal"}},{q="To whom should the orders be returned?",a="They must be brought to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.",al={"who gets the warchief orders","where do i turn in the orders","turn in swamp talker quest"}}},kw={"bengor","blasted lands","fallen hero of the horde","murloc","swamp of sorrows","swamp talker","warchief's orders"},rel={"quest:2622","npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","topic:murloc","topic:horde"},m={start="Bengor",["end"]="Fallen Hero of the Horde",level="55",faction="Horde",id=2623},src={"The Swamp Talker"}}
E["quest:3374"] = {t="quest",n="The Essence of Eranikus",z="swampofsorrows",s="You engage the Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight, and Itharius speaks straight into your mind. Taking up the charge means helping Ysera's Dragonflight redeem the corrupted soul of Eranikus, and the first sacrifice is to give Itharius the gem that chains the part of Eranikus' mind that is still free. Itharius waits in the Swamp of Sorrows.",h="You engage the Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight, and Itharius speaks straight into your mind.",sec={{t="A Voice Through the Stone",b="Through the Oathstone, Itharius tells you that accepting this charge means aiding Ysera's Dragonflight to redeem the corrupted soul of Eranikus. Itharius expects many sacrifices from the two of you, and the first is to hand over the gem that has bound whatever free-willed part of Eranikus' mind remains. The Oathstone and the Chained Essence of Eranikus must go to Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows, and there you choose whether to aid the dragonflight.",sp=0},{t="A Choice Made",b="Itharius greets you at yet another crossroads and asks what choice you make. Once it is made, Itharius says your choices so far have been the correct ones, and that your actions from here on will decide whether that continues.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Itharius?",a="Itharius speaks into your mind through the Oathstone for Ysera's Dragonflight, and waits in the Swamp of Sorrows, seeking to redeem the corrupted soul of Eranikus.",al={"who is itharius","itharius role","who sends the message"}},{q="What is the Chained Essence of Eranikus?",a="It is the gem that chains the part of Eranikus' mind that is still free. Itharius asks you to give it up as the first sacrifice.",al={"chained essence of eranikus","what is the chained gem","eranikus essence"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="It follows the first step of The Essence of Eranikus, under the same name.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous step"}},{q="Where do you take the Oathstone and the essence?",a="To Itharius, in the Swamp of Sorrows, where you choose whether to aid the dragonflight.",al={"where to bring oathstone","where is itharius","hand in location"}}},kw={"chained essence","eranikus","green dragonflight","itharius","oathstone","swamp of sorrows","ysera"},rel={"quest:3512","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight",["end"]="Itharius",level="55",id=3374},src={"The Essence of Eranikus (2)"}}
E["quest:3512"] = {t="quest",n="In Eranikus' Own Words",z="swampofsorrows",s="Itharius wants to find a way of speaking with Eranikus through the gem. Eranikus lies somewhere between sleep and death, caught in a weave of nightmares, and the essence you gave is badly tainted, yet a chance remains. Itharius sends you far off, to eastern Winterspring.",h="Itharius wants to find a way of speaking with Eranikus through the gem.",sec={{t="A Voice Across the Nightmare",b="Itharius explains that Eranikus lies between sleep and death, twisted within a weave of nightmares. The essence you gave is badly tainted, yet there is a chance of reaching him. To open a conversation through the gem, Itharius sends you to eastern Winterspring, a land of ice, to seek one of their mortal allies.",sp=0},{t="The Spiritspeaker",b="The ally is Umbranse the Spiritspeaker, a human who acts as a medium for the dead. Eranikus is not truly dead, but Itharius believes Umbranse may help all the same.",sp=0},{t="Umbranse's Condition",b="Umbranse says Itharius was wise to send you, and that Eranikus will soon offer counsel in his own words. For now Umbranse cannot help directly. Umbranse will lend skill at death-speaking, but first needs the help of someone not held back by the frailties of age, since the most potent augury device in Umbranse's keeping has been taken against Umbranse's will, and without it Eranikus cannot be helped.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this journey?",a="Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows, after taking the tainted essence of Eranikus from you.",al={"who gives in eranikus own words","eranikus quest giver"}},{q="Who is Umbranse the Spiritspeaker?",a="A human who acts as a medium for the dead, and one of Itharius' mortal allies. He is found in eastern Winterspring.",al={"who is umbranse","umbranse spiritspeaker lore"}},{q="Is Eranikus considered dead?",a="Not truly dead. Eranikus lies somewhere between sleep and death, caught in a weave of nightmares.",al={"is eranikus dead","eranikus state of being"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the storyline?",a="It follows the second step of The Essence of Eranikus, in which you gave Itharius the gem holding what remained of Eranikus' free will.",al={"eranikus quest chain order","what came before in eranikus own words"}}},kw={"eranikus","itharius","nightmare","spiritspeaker","swamp of sorrows","umbranse","winterspring"},rel={"quest:3374","zone:winterspring","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:human"},m={start="Itharius",["end"]="Umbranse the Spiritspeaker",level="55",id=3512},src={"In Eranikus' Own Words"}}
E["quest:698"] = {t="quest",n="Lack of Surplus",z="swampofsorrows",s="Dar is gathering supplies for the outpost by the beach in the east, where Tok'Kar has little time to spare between guard shifts and cooking for the soldiers. Dar asks you to bring Tok'Kar a shipment of sawtooth meat.",h="Dar is gathering supplies for the outpost by the beach in the east, where Tok'Kar has little time to spare...",sec={{t="Supplies for the Shore",b="Dar is collecting supplies for the outpost by the beach in the east. Tok'Kar does what is possible there, but guard shifts and cooking for the soldiers leave little time in the day. The soldiers enjoy cooking sawtooth meat when they can get it, and Dar has had no time to send them another shipment.",sp=0},{t="Choosing the Meat",b="Dar warns you to leave the young sawtooths alone, for the older ones taste better. The young need a year or two to reach full size. Eight unprepared sawtooth flanks are wanted, brought to Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is requesting the sawtooth meat?",a="Dar, who is gathering supplies for the outpost by the beach in the east.",al={"who gives lack of surplus","who starts lack of surplus","dar swamp of sorrows"}},{q="Where is Tok'Kar stationed?",a="At the outpost by the beach in the east that Dar speaks of. The meat is to be delivered to Tok'Kar there, in the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"where is tok'kar","tokkar location","tok'kar outpost"}},{q="Why does Tok'Kar need others to bring meat?",a="Between guard shifts and cooking for the soldiers, Tok'Kar has little time left in the day.",al={"why does tok'kar need meat","why does dar send food"}},{q="Which sawtooths should be hunted?",a="The older ones. The young are less tasty, and need a year or two to reach full size.",al={"which sawtooths","what sawtooths drop meat","sawtooth flank source"}},{q="How many flanks are needed?",a="Eight unprepared sawtooth flanks, brought to Tok'Kar.",al={"how many flanks","unprepared sawtooth flank count"}},{q="What comes next in the chain?",a="A second step under the same name follows.",al={"next quest lack of surplus","lack of surplus follow up"}}},kw={"dar","flank","meat","outpost","sawtooth","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","quest:699"},m={start="Dar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="40",faction="Horde",id=698},src={"Lack of Surplus"}}
E["quest:699"] = {t="quest",n="Lack of Surplus",z="swampofsorrows",s="Tok'Kar and the soldiers on the coast are stationed to guard Stonard against murlocs, or to send warning when the force is too large. Tok'Kar wants six sawtooth snapper claws and offers one of the outpost's weapons in thanks.",h="Tok'Kar and the soldiers on the coast are stationed to guard Stonard against murlocs, or to send warning when...",sec={{t="Weapons for the Coast",b="With murlocs a threat along the coast, Tok'Kar and the soldiers are posted here to protect Stonard, or to warn it if the force is too large. That leaves little time for rest, and Tok'Kar could use more help. The claws of sawtooth snappers make fine weapons when properly prepared. Tok'Kar asks for six, and offers one of the outpost's weapons in return, grateful for the meat and the company.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for the claws?",a="Tok'Kar, who is stationed along the coast to protect Stonard.",al={"who gives lack of surplus","quest giver","tokkar"}},{q="Why does Tok'Kar need sawtooth snapper claws?",a="Their claws make fine weapons when properly prepared, and Tok'Kar wants six of them.",al={"why claws","sawtooth snapper purpose","weapon claws"}},{q="What threat is the coastal post watching for?",a="Murlocs along the coast. The soldiers are there to protect Stonard, or to warn it if the force is too large.",al={"coastal dangers","murloc attack stonard","what is tokkar watching"}},{q="Where does this lead next?",a="Threat From the Sea follows.",al={"what comes next","next quest","after lack of surplus"}}},kw={"claws","murlocs","sawtooth snapper","stonard","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","quest:698","quest:1422","topic:murloc","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Tok'Kar",["end"]="Tok'Kar",level="42",faction="Horde",id=699},src={"Lack of Surplus (2)"}}
E["subzone:broken-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Broken Hall",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Broken Hall serves as the flooded outer threshold of the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of Sorrows. Shattered when the Great Dragon Aspect Ysera and her flight dragged the grand ziggurat beneath the waters, this ruin now stands deserted as the Atal'ai zealots retreat into deeper sanctums.",h="The Broken Hall serves as the flooded outer threshold of the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of...",sec={{t="Flooded Threshold",b="When the green dragons brought down their wrath upon the Atal'ai priesthood and submerged their unholy ziggurat beneath the Pool of Tears, the outermost architecture bore the brunt of the cataclysm. The floor of the Broken Hall collapsed completely, allowing murky swamp waters to flood the chamber. Because of the damage and submersion, the troll cultists abandoned this entrance hall, withdrawing further into the complex. Adventurers entering the sunken temple must wade through these sodden ruins before mounting the stairs to reach the Hall of Masks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Broken Hall?",a="It is the outermost entry chamber of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, situated right past the flooded submerged entrance beneath the Pool of Tears.",al={"broken hall overview","what is this place","temple entrance hall"}},{q="Why is the Broken Hall flooded and ruined?",a="The chamber was shattered when the green dragonflight dragged the entire temple beneath the marsh waters to halt the summoning of the Blood God Hakkar, breaking the floor and drowning the hall.",al={"why broken hall wet","why is broken hall submerged","who broke the hall"}},{q="Are there any Atal'ai trolls living in this hall?",a="The Broken Hall itself lies largely abandoned. Following the drowning of the upper temple, the Atal'ai cultists withdrew into drier, more defensible chambers deeper within the complex.",al={"enemies in broken hall","is broken hall empty"}},{q="Where do the stairs in the Broken Hall lead?",a="Ascending the stone stairs leading out of the flooded Broken Hall brings explorers directly into the Hall of Masks.",al={"broken hall stairs","broken hall exit","where to go from broken hall"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For trolls who revere the loa, the Broken Hall is a grim reminder of the ruin brought upon Atal'ai zealots who defied the rest of their kind to serve Hakkar the Soulflayer."},kw={"atal'ai","broken hall","hall of masks","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:hall-of-masks","subzone:pool-of-tears","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:troll"},src={"Broken Hall"}}
E["subzone:fallow-sanctuary"] = {t="subzone",n="Fallow Sanctuary",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Fallow Sanctuary is a secluded village hidden deep within the bogs of the Swamp of Sorrows. It serves as home to an isolated tribe of mutated draenei known as the Lost Ones, whose severe grief and homesickness have driven them feral.",h="The Fallow Sanctuary is a secluded village hidden deep within the bogs of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Refuge Lost to Madness",b="Tucked away among the sunken trees of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Fallow Sanctuary was established by stranded Lost Ones seeking a place of their own. Severed from their ancestral world and deformed by dark energies, these wretched outcasts found no peace in the marshland. Over time, relentless sorrow and isolation shattered their sanity, reducing the tribe to a hostile, feral state where they fiercely attack any outsiders who trespass into their village.",sp=0},{t="Vanished Leaders",b="The settlement was once guided by figures like Ongeku and Noboru the Cudgel, though the village's leadership crumbled following their absence and demise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fallow Sanctuary?",a="It is a settlement located in the Swamp of Sorrows inhabited by the Lost Ones, a heavily mutated and tragic branch of draenei who crossed through the Dark Portal.",al={"fallow sanctuary lore","what is this village","lost one camp swamp"}},{q="Why are the Lost Ones here hostile?",a="Trapped on Azeroth and separated from everything they once knew, the Lost Ones here have been driven completely mad by grief and homesickness, rendering them fiercely feral and aggressive toward outsiders.",al={"why do lost ones attack","are lost ones evil","feral lost ones"}},{q="Who leads the Fallow Sanctuary?",a="The tribe previously answered to prominent figures such as Ongeku and Noboru the Cudgel, though their leadership fell apart due to their disappearance and deaths.",al={"who runs fallow sanctuary","noboru","ongeku"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The twisted fate of the Lost Ones demonstrates how dark energies warp living flesh and shatter frail minds."},kw={"fallow sanctuary","lost ones","noboru the cudgel","ongeku","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Fallow Sanctuary"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-masks"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Masks",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Hall of Masks is an ominous chamber inside the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of Sorrows. Lined with giant skull masks and marred by a bone-strewn trench, it marks one of the early thresholds deeper into the Atal'ai stronghold.",h="The Hall of Masks is an ominous chamber inside the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Threshold",b="Located just past the staircase descending from the Broken Hall, the Hall of Masks serves as a central junction within the Sunken Temple. The chamber earns its name from the imposing, stylized skull masks mounted along its stone walls. Below them runs a deep trench choked with discarded bones, suggesting a macabre purpose whose exact nature is unknown. Beyond this eerie hall lie passages branching out to the Butchery, the Chamber of Blood, and the Den of the Caller.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Masks located?",a="The Hall of Masks is an interior wing of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, situated beneath the waters of the Pool of Tears in the Swamp of Sorrows. You reach it by descending past the Broken Hall near the entrance of the sunken complex.",al={"hall of masks location","where is hall of masks","find hall of masks"}},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Masks?",a="It takes its name from the massive carved skull masks that decorate the walls of the chamber, looming over anyone who treads through the temple corridors.",al={"hall of masks name meaning","why masks"}},{q="What was the purpose of the trench in the floor?",a="The trench is littered with bones, suggesting a macabre function. Its exact purpose is unknown.",al={"why are there bones in the floor","hall of masks bone pit","trench of bones"}},{q="Where do the passages from this hall lead?",a="Venturing beyond the Hall of Masks leads deeper into the temple's lower complexes, connecting directly toward areas like the Butchery, the Chamber of Blood, and the Den of the Caller.",al={"hall of masks exits","where does hall of masks lead"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, the chamber represents the sinister lengths to which the Atal'ai zealots were willing to go in their desperate pursuit of Hakkar the Soulflayer.",["class:Priest"]="The macabre architecture and bone-filled trench hint at the dark practices of the Atal'ai, though the chamber's precise use is unknown."},kw={"atal'ai","broken hall","hall of masks","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:broken-hall","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:troll"},src={"Hall of Masks"}}
E["subzone:harborage"] = {t="subzone",n="Harborage",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Harborage is a quiet settlement of exiled Draenor natives situated in the northern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows. While many of their afflicted kin wandering the surrounding bogs have succumbed to madness and primal hostility, the inhabitants here have managed to hold onto their sanity and wits. They live cautiously along the waterline, seeking peace amidst a harsh and unforgiving wilderness.",h="The Harborage is a quiet settlement of exiled Draenor natives situated in the northern reaches of the Swamp...",sec={{t="A Haven in the Mire",b="Tucked away against the northern mountains of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Harborage stands in stark contrast to the feral tribes wandering the nearby waters. Constructed of rugged leather shelters and adorned with mysterious hanging crystals, this small encampment provides sanctuary to exiled Draenor survivors who have refused to surrender their minds. Under the guidance of elders like Magtoor, they maintain a fragile, civilized enclave while remaining watchful of the hostile wilderness, native predators, and the feral tribes of their fallen brothers lurking just beyond their perimeter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Harborage?",a="The Harborage is home to a band of Draenor exiles—afflicted humanoids who crossed into Azeroth and managed to preserve their minds and culture, unlike the feral tribes found elsewhere in the swamp.",al={"harborage residents","who is at harborage","who lives here"}},{q="Why are the people here peaceful while other swamp tribes attack?",a="The residents here retained their sanity and rational thinking despite their tragic physical transformation and displacement. While their afflicted kin across the bog lost their minds to isolation and trauma, those at the Harborage banded together to preserve their dignity.",al={"why are they friendly","lost ones friendly","harborage hostile"}},{q="Who leads the Harborage?",a="The community looks to respected elders like Magtoor for leadership and guidance as they navigate survival in an alien swamp.",al={"harborage leader","magtoor","chief of harborage"}},{q="Where is the Harborage located?",a="You can find it tucked against the northern cliffs of the Swamp of Sorrows, just east of the mountain pass connecting the marsh to the Redridge Mountains.",al={"harborage location","where is harborage","find harborage"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers descending from the safety of Redridge into the dangerous marshlands, the Harborage is one of the few places in the northern swamp that offers non-hostile faces rather than immediate bloodshed.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's presence at Stonard largely dominates the swamp, but these reclusive survivors maintain their own secluded existence, keeping to themselves rather than picking sides in the regional conflicts."},kw={"broken","draenethyst","harborage","lost ones","magtoor","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire"},src={"Harborage"}}
E["subzone:itharius-s-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Itharius's Cave",z="swampofsorrows",s="Itharius's Cave is a secluded hollow tucked into the far southwestern cliffs of the Swamp of Sorrows. It serves as the refuge of the enigmatic Itharius, who appears to be a high elf and tends to the brood of green dragonkin inhabiting the surrounding marsh.",h="Itharius's Cave is a secluded hollow tucked into the far southwestern cliffs of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Hermit Among Whelps",b="Tucked away in the treacherous, moss-draped crags of the southwestern Swamp of Sorrows, this damp cavern shelters the recluse Itharius. Outside its mouth, unruly green whelps wander the mire. Though he appears to be a high elf, a folk who rarely wander so far south into wild swamps alone, Itharius keeps a watchful eye on these young dragonkin as they grow, living alongside them in quiet isolation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in this cave?",a="The cave is home to Itharius, a mysterious hermit who appears to be a high elf. He dwells apart from civilization and watches over the local dragonkin.",al={"who is itharius","cave owner","who lives here"}},{q="Where is Itharius's Cave located?",a="It is tucked deep in the southwestern corner of the Swamp of Sorrows, against the mountain ridges south of the main road.",al={"itharius cave location","where is itharius","how to find cave"}},{q="Why are there green whelps outside the cave?",a="The surrounding marsh is inhabited by green whelps. Itharius has taken it upon himself to watch over and protect these unruly young dragons as they grow.",al={"why whelps here","green dragons swamp of sorrows","whelps outside"}},{q="Why would a high elf live out in the swamp?",a="Itharius appears to be a high elf, a folk rarely seen in these southern bogs, yet he remains here specifically to safeguard the green dragonkin of the swamp, keeping to himself in his remote den.",al={"high elf in swamp","why is itharius here"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The presence of green dragonkin in the swamp makes this cave of particular interest to druids, whose traditions are deeply tied to the Green Dragonflight and the Emerald Dream."},kw={"dragonkin","green whelps","high elf","itharius","itharius's cave","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Itharius's Cave"}}
E["subzone:misty-reed-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Reed Post",z="swampofsorrows",s="Misty Reed Post is a rugged Horde encampment situated between Stagalbog and the Misty Reed Strand in the eastern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows. Established as a frontline watch under the authority of Stonard, it serves to monitor the dangerous wetlands and the treacherous coastline.",h="Misty Reed Post is a rugged Horde encampment situated between Stagalbog and the Misty Reed Strand in the...",sec={{t="A Lonely Outpost",b="Tucked away in the humid gloom between the Stagalbog and the eastern shore, Misty Reed Post is little more than a spartan camp under Stonard's banner. It is manned by a handful of Stonard hunters, a shaman, Katar, and Tok'Kar, who oversees the watch. Conditions are rough, offering no fortified shelter from the marsh's hostile wildlife and lingering damp. Tok'Kar harbors quiet ambitions that the Horde command in Stonard will one day reinforce the position with a sturdy orcish burrow or watchtower, though for now, the scouts must hold the marsh with tents, campfire smoke, and sharpened steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Misty Reed Post?",a="It serves as a secondary forward camp for the Horde garrison at Stonard. Stationed between the wetlands of Stagalbog and the coast of the Misty Reed Strand, its sentries keep watch over coastal threats and native swamp beasts.",al={"why is misty reed post here","misty reed post purpose","what is this camp"}},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="The post is led by Tok'Kar, an orc tasked with holding the vulnerable camp alongside Katar, a Stonard shaman, and several Stonard hunters. Tok'Kar hopes the settlement will eventually be granted the resources to construct permanent fortifications.",al={"who leads misty reed post","tokkar","tok'kar"}},{q="Is there a flight master at Misty Reed Post?",a="No. Misty Reed Post is an austere field encampment without wind rider facilities. Travelers seeking flight paths must make the journey west along the road to Stonard.",al={"misty reed flight path","is there a flight path here","flight master misty reed post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The camp offers a welcome pocket of safety and local guidance for Horde scouts navigating the perilous eastern edges of the marsh.",["class:Hunter"]="Staffed primarily by Stonard hunters who know the surrounding marsh ecology, the post represents the grit needed to track and survive amidst hostile wetland predators."},kw={"katar","misty reed post","misty reed strand","stagalbog","stonard","swamp of sorrows","tok'kar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:misty-reed-strand","subzone:stagalbog","topic:horde"},src={"Misty Reed Post"}}
E["subzone:misty-reed-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Reed Strand",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Misty Reed Strand is the fog-shrouded, desolate eastern coastline of the Swamp of Sorrows. Lined with jagged rocks, washed-up wreckage, and creeping swamp mist, it is home to aggressive crabs, crocolisks, and coastal murloc tribes. Travelers venturing down to the surf often find themselves contending with the local wildlife for whatever resources wash ashore.",h="The Misty Reed Strand is the fog-shrouded, desolate eastern coastline of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Foggy Shoreline",b="Stretching along the entire eastern border of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Misty Reed Strand forms a damp barrier between the deep mire and the Great Sea. Heavy mists constantly roll in off the water, obscuring vision and muffling the cries of native wildlife. The beaches are littered with sea debris, driftwood, and decaying vegetation washed out from the bog inland. Because of its remote position and harsh climate, no formal permanent settlements hold the shoreline, leaving the sands to aggressive crustaceans, stalking crocolisks, and territorial murlocs who violently defend their foraging grounds.",sp=0},{t="Contested Waters",b="Both Alliance and Horde scouts periodically direct adventurers out to the strands, though neither faction claims the beach as sovereign territory. The Alliance often gathers driftwood and beach salvage here while attempting to thin the skittering crab population. Meanwhile, Horde outposts further inland keep a wary eye on the coastline's murloc encampments, sending seasoned fighters to cull their numbers before the amphibious raiders can push deeper toward Stonard or threaten marsh travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Reed Strand located?",a="The Misty Reed Strand runs along the far eastern edge of the Swamp of Sorrows, bordering the Great Sea. It can be reached by traveling directly east through the wetlands from either Stonard or the surrounding marsh paths.",al={"where is misty reed strand","misty reed strand location","how to get to misty reed strand"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the strand?",a="The shoreline is heavily populated by giant coastal crabs, swamp crocolisks, and various tribes of hostile murlocs scavenging the tide lines.",al={"monsters at misty reed strand","what lives on misty reed strand","misty reed strand enemies"}},{q="Are there any settlements on the beach?",a="There are no permanent friendly towns or established military outposts along the beach itself. The nearest settlements are located deeper inland within the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"towns near misty reed strand","misty reed strand base","friendly camps misty reed strand"}},{q="Why do the factions send adventurers to the Misty Reed Strand?",a="Both the Alliance and Horde occasionally send mercenaries to the coast. Alliance emissaries often look for salvaged driftwood and coastal materials, while Horde forces dispatch warriors to cull the aggressive murloc tribes living on the surf.",al={"why go to misty reed strand","misty reed strand quests"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling south from Nethergarde or traversing the marshlands often scavenge the beach's abundant driftwood and resources while keeping its aggressive wildlife at bay.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonard's defenders view the murloc tribes of the strand as an unmanaged threat, frequently ordering combat patrols to purge their encampments along the surf."},kw={"beach","coast","crocolisk","driftwood","great sea","misty reed strand","murloc","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Misty Reed Strand"}}
E["subzone:misty-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Valley",z="swampofsorrows",s="Tucked away in the northwestern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Misty Valley is a shadowed, fog-drenched hollow north of the pass into Deadwind. The secluded basin is overrun by primordial swamp beasts, wandering swampwalkers, and tangled horrors. Deep in its rearmost cave dwells the colossal and terrifying Mire Lord.",h="Tucked away in the northwestern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows, the Misty Valley is a shadowed, fog-drenched...",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Glen",b="Nestled beneath the high cliffs separating the Swamp of Sorrows from Deadwind Pass, the Misty Valley is perpetually choked with thick marsh vapor. Unlike the open wetlands to the east, this isolated pocket is dense with colossal marsh elementals, including looming swampwalkers, ancient swampwalker elders, and creeping tangled horrors. At the far end of the misty gorge lies a cavern that serves as the lair of the Mire Lord, one of the most formidable natural threats haunting the bog.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Valley located?",a="The Misty Valley is situated in the far northwestern corner of the Swamp of Sorrows, directly north of the road that leads up into Deadwind Pass.",al={"misty valley location","where is misty valley","misty valley swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What creatures inhabit this valley?",a="The valley is overrun by colossal plant elementals and marsh horrors, specifically swampwalkers, elder swampwalkers, and tangled horrors that wander through the thick fog.",al={"misty valley mobs","what lives in misty valley","enemies in misty valley"}},{q="What is inside the cave at the back of the valley?",a="Deep within the cave at the rear of the Misty Valley dwells the Mire Lord, a massive and powerful marsh elemental that reigns over the secluded hollow.",al={"misty valley cave","mire lord cave","who is in misty valley cave"}},{q="Is the Misty Valley safe to traverse?",a="Not at all. The towering swampwalkers and tangled horrors that roam the dense fog are hostile and aggressive, making the valley hazardous for unwary travelers venturing off the main road.",al={"is misty valley dangerous","misty valley level"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The hulking swampwalkers and tangled horrors inhabiting this secluded valley represent the wild, untamed fury of marsh elementals deeply entwined with the primordial nature of the swamp."},kw={"deadwind pass","mire lord","misty valley","swamp of sorrows","swampwalker","tangled horror"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:deadwind"},src={"Misty Valley"}}
E["subzone:pool-of-tears"] = {t="subzone",n="Pool of Tears",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Pool of Tears is a large, murky lake dominating the eastern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows. Deep beneath its surface lies the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar, brought low by the Green Dragonflight to contain the horrors within. Today, vicious frenzies patrol the turbid waters, and ancient troll ruins litter its drowned banks.",h="The Pool of Tears is a large, murky lake dominating the eastern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Drowned Sanctuary",b="Long ago, fanatical Atal'ai trolls raised a monumental ziggurat to their bloodthirsty god, Hakkar the Soulflayer. Horrified by the blasphemies taking place within, the Dragon Aspect Ysera shattered the ground beneath the structure, submerging the massive temple into the depths of the marsh. The existing lake flooded over the temple ruins. While the dragons sought to bury the evil forever, the ziggurat still stands beneath the silt and waves, and green drakes remain vigilant in the area to keep its corruption sealed.",sp=0},{t="Waters of Peril",b="Navigating the murky lake is treacherous for any adventurer heading toward the sunken halls. Flesh-eating frenzies infest the waters, while Atal'ai artifacts and drowned stonework remain scattered across the muddy floor. Travelers must brave these hostile shallows to access the upper passages of the submerged temple, where cultists and lingering dragon guardians vie for control of the dark sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Pool of Tears?",a="The origin of the name is not recorded. The lake is known for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, which Ysera sank beneath its waters to halt the summoning of Hakkar.",al={"pool of tears name origin","why pool of tears","pool of tears meaning"}},{q="What is the massive building in the center of the lake?",a="It is the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, often called the Sunken Temple. Once a towering Atal'ai ziggurat, it was cast beneath the waters by Ysera and remains partially submerged in the center of the pool.",al={"building in pool of tears","ruins in lake swamp of sorrows","sunken temple location"}},{q="Why are there green dragons around the water?",a="Ysera's brood arrived to destroy the temple and drown its vile ceremonies. Green drakes and dragonkin still watch over the lake to ensure the Atal'ai cultists cannot finish their summoning of the Blood God.",al={"green dragons swamp of sorrows","why are dragons here","ysera temple lake"}},{q="Is it safe to swim across the pool?",a="No. The lake is infested with aggressive, flesh-eating frenzies that will attack anyone swimming out toward the temple entrance.",al={"pool of tears swimming","sharks in pool of tears","frenzies swamp of sorrows"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For darkspear trolls, the pool serves as a grim warning of what happens when trollkind embraces forbidden blood magic like that of the Atal'ai.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold reverence for the lake, recognizing it as a site where Ysera and the Green Dragonflight intervened to stem the taint of the Blood God."},kw={"atal'ai","frenzies","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar","ysera"},rel={"subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Pool of Tears"}}
E["subzone:shifting-mire"] = {t="subzone",n="Shifting Mire",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Shifting Mire forms the vast, muddy heart of the Swamp of Sorrows, lying just west of the Pool of Tears. Its name comes from the strange, restless silt beneath the murky water, which seems to drift and gather under the influence of an unseen force.",h="The Shifting Mire forms the vast, muddy heart of the Swamp of Sorrows, lying just west of the Pool of Tears.",sec={{t="A Living Bog",b="Spanning the central reaches of the marshland, the Shifting Mire is an unsettling expanse where solid footing is hard to come by. The silt along the swamp floor shifts and collects as though moved by a living will, driven by a strange, ambient energy permeating the peat. Amidst the drifting mud prowl predatory swamp jaguars, massive sorrow spinners, and hungry sawtooth crocolisks, while bands of broken draenei known as the Lost Ones stalk the sunken paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Shifting Mire?",a="The area takes its name from the extremely fine silt resting along the bog floor. Instead of settling like normal sediment, a mysterious current of energy causes the mud to gather, drift, and flow across the wetlands as if it were alive.",al={"shifting mire name origin","why shifting mire","why does the ground move"}},{q="What creatures live in the Shifting Mire?",a="The mire is overrun with dangerous wildlife, including sawtooth crocolisks lurking in the shallows, giant sorrow spinners weaving webs in the boughs, and stealthy swamp jaguars. It is also frequented by roaming Lost Ones, draenei warped and exiled from their homeworld.",al={"shifting mire mobs","what is in shifting mire"}},{q="Where is the Shifting Mire located?",a="It encompasses the central expanse of the Swamp of Sorrows, positioned directly to the west of the massive lake known as the Pool of Tears.",al={"shifting mire location","where is shifting mire"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The tangled brush and drifting waters make tracking treacherous, requiring hunters to stay sharp against stealthy swamp jaguars and venomous sorrow spinners hiding in the foliage."},kw={"crocolisks","jaguars","lost ones","shifting mire","silt","sorrow spinners","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears"},src={"Shifting Mire"}}
E["subzone:sorrowmurk"] = {t="subzone",n="Sorrowmurk",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Sorrowmurk is the treacherous wetland expanse lying directly east of the Pool of Tears in the Swamp of Sorrows. Long dominated by patrolling green dragonkin guarding the approach to the Sunken Temple, it remains one of the most perilous regions in the eastern marshes.",h="The Sorrowmurk is the treacherous wetland expanse lying directly east of the Pool of Tears in the Swamp of...",sec={{t="A Perilous Border",b="Stretching out along the eastern edge of the Pool of Tears, the Sorrowmurk is a dense and murky mire that borders the Forbidding Sea. For years, the waters and tangled boughs have crawled with ferocious green dragonspawn and towering drakes, remnants of the brood sent to watch over the submerged temple of Atal'Hakkar. Their presence ensures that only seasoned travelers dare wander through its sodden reaches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Sorrowmurk located?",a="The Sorrowmurk lies in the easternmost section of the Swamp of Sorrows, just beyond the Pool of Tears and the sunken ruins of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, bordering the coast.",al={"sorrowmurk location","where is sorrowmurk","sorrowmurk map"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the Sorrowmurk?",a="The region is notorious for green dragonkin, including aggressive dragonspawn and large drakes that fiercely patrol the marsh around the temple waters.",al={"sorrowmurk mobs","what lives in sorrowmurk","sorrowmurk enemies"}},{q="Why are there green dragons in the Sorrowmurk?",a="The Green Dragonflight was tasked by Ysera to watch over the Pool of Tears and ensure that the evil sunken within the Temple of Atal'Hakkar remained contained.",al={"why dragons here","green dragonflight swamp of sorrows","temple dragons"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The sorrowful corruption touching the Emerald Dream's guardians in these wetlands makes the green dragonkin here a tragic sight for any servant of nature."},kw={"atal'hakkar","dragonspawn","green dragonflight","green drake","pool of tears","sorrowmurk","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears"},src={"Sorrowmurk"}}
E["subzone:splinterspear-junction"] = {t="subzone",n="Splinterspear Junction",z="swampofsorrows",s="Splinterspear Junction is a strategic fork in the main road winding through the heart of the Swamp of Sorrows. Dominated by a rugged orc watchtower and regularly patrolled by Horde sentries, it divides the path between northern retreats and southern outposts.",h="Splinterspear Junction is a strategic fork in the main road winding through the heart of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Conflict",b="Standing near the center of the Swamp of Sorrows, Splinterspear Junction divides travelers between two paths: the northern trail leading toward the Lost One refuge of the Harborage and the Fallow Sanctuary, and the southern road running directly past the fortress of Stonard toward the Blasted Lands. An ancient orcish watchtower oversees the split, garrisoned and patrolled by active Horde troops. For members of the Horde, it serves as a secure landmark in a treacherous marsh; for Alliance travelers, it represents a deadly ambush point along an already unforgiving trail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the roads at Splinterspear Junction lead?",a="The road splits into two distinct routes. The northern fork leads past the Draenei haven of the Harborage and toward the Fallow Sanctuary, while the southern branch directs travelers south to Stonard and onward into the parched wastes of the Blasted Lands.",al={"where does the road go","splinterspear paths","which way at splinterspear"}},{q="Is Splinterspear Junction safe for Alliance travelers?",a="No. The junction is held by the Horde, who maintain a fortified watchtower and regular patrols around the intersection. These guards are openly hostile to the Alliance and will flag passing adventurers for combat on sight.",al={"alliance safe splinterspear","are guards hostile","splinterspear pvp"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Tread carefully around the junction; the orcish watchtower is heavily guarded by Horde sentries eager to cut down any intruders straying from Darkshire.",["faction:Horde"]="The watchtower at the junction provides a vital waypoint and security checkpoint when traveling between Stonard and northern destinations in the swamp."},kw={"harborage","splinterspear junction","stonard","swamp of sorrows","watchtower"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stonard","subzone:harborage","subzone:fallow-sanctuary","zone:blastedlands","topic:horde"},src={"Splinterspear Junction"}}
E["subzone:stagalbog"] = {t="subzone",n="Stagalbog",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Stagalbog is a dense, waterlogged marsh stretch across the southern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows. Bordering the southern mountain range just below the Pool of Tears, it remains an untamed wilderness.",h="The Stagalbog is a dense, waterlogged marsh stretch across the southern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="The Southern Mire",b="Stretching beneath the shadow of the southern crags, the Stagalbog is typical of the Swamp of Sorrows: stagnant water, drooping reeds, and tangled vegetation. It sits immediately south of the sunken ruins of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, caught between the tainted lake and the rocky boundary of the region. Apart from rough wildlife, civilization has established no foothold here.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of the Temple",b="Because it borders the Pool of Tears, the Stagalbog frequently catches whatever shadows or corruptions seep from the Sunken Temple.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stagalbog located?",a="The Stagalbog is located in the southern part of the Swamp of Sorrows, situated directly south of the Pool of Tears and running along the base of the southern mountain range.",al={"stagalbog location","where is stagalbog","how to find stagalbog"}},{q="What threats can be found wandering the bog?",a="The bog is inhabited by indigenous marsh beasts and predatory creatures.",al={"stagalbog mobs","monsters in stagalbog"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, sun-deprived roots of the Stagalbog provide prime growing conditions for swamp flora that thrive away from trodden paths.",["class:Hunter"]="The quiet swaths between the marsh water and the mountain cliffs make the Stagalbog a prime stalking ground for native swamp beasts."},kw={"marsh","pool of tears","stagalbog","stagalbog cave","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:stagalbog-cave","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar"},src={"Stagalbog"}}
E["subzone:stagalbog-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Stagalbog Cave",z="swampofsorrows",s="Stagalbog Cave is a damp subterranean cavern situated in the Stagalbog within the eastern reaches of the Swamp of Sorrows. It serves as a fortified den for the Marsh murlocs and their sinister spiritual leader, the Swamp Talker.",h="Stagalbog Cave is a damp subterranean cavern situated in the Stagalbog within the eastern reaches of the...",sec={{t="Den of the Marsh Tribe",b="Tucked away in the murky eastern wetlands of the Swamp of Sorrows, Stagalbog Cave provides shelter from the relentless swamp rains for the local murlocs. Known as the Marsh tribe, these amphibious creatures aggressively guard the winding cavern chambers alongside their chief mystic, the Swamp Talker. Travelers venturing near the sunken mire of the Stagalbog often hear their gurgling calls echoing out across the mossy banks, warning trespassers away from their nesting grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Stagalbog Cave?",a="Stagalbog Cave is a natural cavern located in the Stagalbog within the eastern region of the Swamp of Sorrows. It is primarily occupied by a vicious settlement of Marsh murlocs.",al={"where is stagalbog cave","what's in stagalbog cave"}},{q="Who rules the cave?",a="The cavern is dominated by the Marsh tribe and their leader, the Swamp Talker, an influential murloc mystic who oversees the tribe's rituals and defenses within the damp interior.",al={"stagalbog boss","swamp talker","who leads the murlocs here"}},{q="Are there friendly settlements nearby?",a="The cave is surrounded by wild, hostile marshlands. The nearest friendly settlement, for the Horde at least, is the outpost of Stonard to the west.",al={"nearest town","vendors near stagalbog"}}},kw={"marsh murlocs","murloc den","stagalbog","stagalbog cave","swamp of sorrows","swamp talker"},rel={"subzone:stagalbog","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},src={"Stagalbog Cave"}}
E["subzone:stonard"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonard",z="swampofsorrows",s="Stonard is a fortified Horde outpost situated in the southern marshes of the Swamp of Sorrows. Originally built during the First War, it serves the modern Horde as an essential foothold in the southern Eastern Kingdoms and an observation post watching the Blasted Lands.",h="Stonard is a fortified Horde outpost situated in the southern marshes of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Relic of the First War",b="Stonard stands as one of the oldest orcish settlements on Azeroth. First established when the Old Horde spilled through the Dark Portal into what was once the Black Morass, Stonard and its sister post, Rockard, anchored the invaders' lines. Though abandoned and damaged during the fallout of the Second War, Thrall's New Horde moved to reconstruct and garrison Stonard. Anchored by a traditional orcish Great Hall and fortified burrows, the outpost is now a vital island of Horde authority in an untamed, perilous mire.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Outpost",b="Modern Stonard functions as both an expeditionary camp and a staging ground. Cartographers and scouts fan out across the surrounding muck to map the uncharted swamp and monitor hostile native beasts, lost draenei wanderers, and the sunken Temple of Atal'Hakkar to the east. Crucially, Stonard also provides the Horde with an organized staging post just north of the shattered Blasted Lands, ensuring a watchful eye remains near the dormant Dark Portal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stonard important to the Horde?",a="Stonard gives the Horde a fortified military and logistics hub deep in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. It allows scouts to chart the hazardous Swamp of Sorrows, provides a base of operations for assaults on the nearby Sunken Temple, and keeps a standing garrison close to the Blasted Lands.",al={"why is stonard here","stonard purpose","what is stonard"}},{q="How old is Stonard?",a="It dates back to the First War, making it one of the earliest orc settlements established on Azeroth. Founded by the Old Horde shortly after they passed through the Dark Portal, it fell into disuse following the Second War before Thrall's New Horde rebuilt it.",al={"stonard history","when was stonard built","who founded stonard"}},{q="What happened to its sister settlement, Rockard?",a="Rockard was established alongside Stonard during the First War, and the two sister towns anchored the Old Horde's lines in the swamp. Unlike Stonard, which the new Horde has rebuilt, Rockard's fate since the wars is not recorded.",al={"what is rockard","rockard history","stonard sister town"}},{q="Can you fly or travel directly to Stonard?",a="Yes. Stonard maintains flight paths connecting it across the continent to Kargath, Flame Crest, Grom'gol Base Camp, the neutral port of Booty Bay, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",al={"stonard flight path","how to get to stonard","stonard portals"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Stonard is renowned as the primary enclave in the southern Eastern Kingdoms where Horde shamans can find guidance and training far away from Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Stonard serves as the Horde's solitary, fortified anchor point between the Badlands to the north and Stranglethorn Vale to the west."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","great hall","orcs","rockard","stonard","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","zone:blastedlands","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:kargath","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp","topic:old-horde","topic:new-horde"},src={"Stonard"}}
E["subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar"] = {t="subzone",n="Temple of Atal'Hakkar",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar, widely known as the Sunken Temple, is a submerged fortress built by exiled troll priests dedicated to the blood god Hakkar. Sunk beneath the marshes by the green dragonflight centuries ago, its drowned halls remain a staging ground for forbidden rituals and dark corruption.",h="The Temple of Atal'Hakkar, widely known as the Sunken Temple, is a submerged fortress built by exiled troll...",sec={{t="Wrath of the Green Flight",b="Over a millennium ago, a catastrophic civil war shattered the Gurubashi Empire when the Atal'ai priesthood attempted to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer. Exiled to the north, the surviving zealots raised a massive stone temple in the Swamp of Sorrows to finish their dark work. Learning of their scheme, the Dragon Aspect Ysera smashed the ziggurat deep into the mire, inundating its chambers beneath the Pool of Tears. Green dragon wardens were left behind to guard the drowned ruins and ensure Hakkar's return was thwarted forever.",sp=0},{t="A Slumber Turned Nightmare",b="Instead of burying the cult, the temple's submersion provided the Atal'ai isolation to continue their grisly sacrifices unhindered. Over the centuries, corruption began to rot the guardians from within; the dragon sentinels succumb to madness while the Atal'ai, guided by Jammal'an the Prophet, prepare the way for Hakkar's avatar. Now, both the Horde and Alliance keep an anxious eye on the submerged ziggurat as shadowy rumors slip out from the swamp's depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the temple underwater?",a="Ysera, the Aspect of the green dragonflight, personally crushed the temple beneath the waters of the marsh to stop the Atal'ai trolls from summoning the blood god Hakkar into Azeroth.",al={"why sunken temple","who sunk the temple","how did it sink"}},{q="Who are the Atal'ai?",a="The Atal'ai are a fanatic sect of troll priests exiled from the southern Gurubashi Empire for practicing blood magic and attempting to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer into the physical realm.",al={"atalai lore","who built the sunken temple","atal'ai priests"}},{q="Why are there green dragons here?",a="Ysera assigned a flight of green dragons to watch over the sunken ruins and keep trespassers out, ensuring Hakkar could never be summoned. Tragically, many of these guardians have fallen prey to madness and dark corruption.",al={"why dragons in swamp","green dragonflight sunken temple"}},{q="How do you get inside the temple?",a="You must swim into the flooded ruins from the Pool of Tears, navigating the submerged passageways of the Broken Hall and ascending through stone corridors like the Hall of Masks.",al={"how to enter sunken temple","sunken temple entrance","getting into atal hakkar"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, the ruins are a grim reminder of the blood-soaked madness that ruined the ancient Gurubashi Empire and the eternal danger of Hakkar the Soulflayer.",["class:Druid"]="The corruption of Ysera's green dragon wardens in the temple's depths strikes at the heart of the Emerald Dream, demanding swift investigation."},kw={"atal'ai","atal'hakkar","eranikus","hakkar","jammal'an","pool of tears","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","ysera"},rel={"zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:broken-hall","subzone:hall-of-masks","topic:troll","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:explorers-league","npc:thrall"},src={"Temple of Atal'Hakkar"}}
E["zone:swampofsorrows"] = {t="zone",n="Swamp of Sorrows",z="swampofsorrows",s="The Swamp of Sorrows is a murky, brackish wetland tucked between Deadwind Pass and the arid Blasted Lands. Once the northern expanse of the ancient Black Morass, its salt-crusted bogs are home to dangerous wildlife, green dragonspawn, and the ruined Temple of Atal'Hakkar sunken beneath the Pool of Tears. While the Horde maintains the fortified garrison of Stonard, the Alliance has no safe haven within the mire, leaving the wilderness largely untamed.",h="The Swamp of Sorrows is a murky, brackish wetland tucked between Deadwind Pass and the arid Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Drowned History",b="Long before the coming of the Orcish Horde, these marshes formed the northern half of an enormous wetlands known as the Black Morass. Following the shattering of the Gurubashi Empire, the fanatical Atal'ai trolls fled into the mire to erect the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, intending to summon their bloodthirsty loa, Hakkar the Soulflayer. Sensing the catastrophe, the Aspect Ysera unleashed her powers, drowning the cursed pyramid beneath the waters of the Pool of Tears. Green dragonflight guardians led by Eranikus were stationed to vigilantly watch over the drowned structure. When the Dark Portal's cataclysm later scorched the southern morass into the Blasted Lands, this northern fen earned its current sorrowful name.",sp=0},{t="Outposts and Broken Exiles",b="Stonard serves as the primary civilized foothold in the swamp. Originally established during the First War alongside the now-ruined settlements of Rockard and Kyross, the outpost was rebuilt under Thrall to serve as the Horde's southernmost staging ground in the Eastern Kingdoms. Beyond Stonard's palisades, strange wanderers roam the fen. A group of draenei stragglers stranded on Azeroth succumbed to homesickness and madness, degenerating into feral Lost Ones. However, a small enclave of lucid Broken exiles persists at the Harborage, wary but willing to trade peacefully with travelers.",sp=0},{t="The Sinking Mire",b="Surviving the swamp requires constant vigilance against its predatory wildlife. Deep bogs hide lunging crocolisks, venomous spiders, prowling swamp jaguars, and wandering bog beasts encrusted with marsh debris. Coastal caverns and the Misty Reed Strand crawl with vicious murlocs, while the salt-laden tide creeps continually inland, preserving rotten logs in thick briny crusts. Farther east lies Sorrowmurk, where aggressive elite dragonspawn fiercely guard the approaches to the Sunken Temple, attacking anyone who strays near their vigil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I reach the Swamp of Sorrows?",a="The most common overland route leads east from Darkshire in Duskwood, through the perilous haunted defile of Deadwind Pass, and straight down into the marsh. Alternatively, travelers coming from the south can walk north along the main road out of the Blasted Lands.",al={"how to get to swamp of sorrows","swamp of sorrows road","getting to stonard"}},{q="Why is the Temple of Atal'Hakkar underwater?",a="Centuries ago, the Atal'ai priesthood tried to summon Hakkar the Soulflayer into Azeroth. Ysera, the Dragon Aspect of the Green Flight, discovered their demonic blood rites and drowned the entire temple into the bog to avert the disaster, leaving behind green dragonspawn to guard the submerged halls.",al={"why is sunken temple sunk","who sank the temple","sunken temple lore"}},{q="What is Stonard?",a="Stonard was one of the first settlements built by the Orcish Horde after crossing through the Dark Portal during the First War. Though ravaged during the fighting, it was recently reclaimed and rebuilt under Thrall's orders to anchor Horde logistics near the Blasted Lands.",al={"stonard history","orc base in swamp","who built stonard"}},{q="Are there any Alliance settlements here?",a="No. The Alliance maintains no towns, guards, or flight paths in the Swamp of Sorrows. Alliance adventurers operating in the area must base themselves out of Darkshire in Duskwood to the west or Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands to the south.",al={"alliance base swamp of sorrows","alliance flight path swamp","where is alliance camp"}},{q="Who are the strange mutated humanoids in the swamp?",a="They are draenei who were stranded on Azeroth following the collapse of the Dark Portal. Severed from their world, most went mad from despair and turned into hostile Lost Ones. A small pocket of sane Broken exiles took refuge in the northwest at the Harborage, choosing neutral survival over mindless rage.",al={"who are the lost ones","what is the harborage","draenei in swamp"}},{q="What is Sorrowmurk?",a="Sorrowmurk is the dense tract of marshland directly east of the Pool of Tears. It serves as a patrol ground for elite green dragonspawn and whelps who violently turn away mortals to safeguard the secrets of the Sunken Temple.",al={"dragon area swamp of sorrows","sorrowmurk dragons","green dragonspawn swamp"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stonard serves as your vital forward redoubt in the southern continent, hosting direct wyvern routes to Kargath, Flame Crest, Grom'gol Base Camp, Booty Bay, and Rog'mar in the Riverglades.",["faction:Alliance"]="Without an outpost to rally behind, traveling through the swamp is an isolated, hostile venture requiring careful preparation from Darkshire or Nethergarde Keep.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The marsh is one of the few places in Azeroth rich in blindweed, alongside generous growths of liferoot, fadeleaf, and stranglekelp.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Tough adventurers can gather iron, gold, mithril, and truesilver along the mountainous crags framing the swamp's northern and southern edges.",["race:Troll"]="The sunken ruins of Atal'Hakkar stand as a dire reminder of the dark blood magic that fractured the Gurubashi Empire and drew the wrath of the Dragon Aspects."},kw={"black morass","broken","harborage","lost ones","pool of tears","sorrowmurk","stonard","sunken temple","swamp of sorrows","temple of atal'hakkar"},rel={"subzone:stonard","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","subzone:pool-of-tears","subzone:harborage","subzone:sorrowmurk","zone:blastedlands","npc:fel-zerul"},src={"Swamp of Sorrows (Classic)","Swamp of Sorrows"}}
